{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"searching","title":"Searching","group":"","order":5,"html":"<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]</p>\n</div>\n<p>x = 2</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p>O/P = 1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef binary(l,x):\n  low = 0\n  high = len(l) - 1\n  while low &lt;= high:\n    mid = (low + high) // 2\n    if l[mid] == x:\n      return mid\n    elif l[mid] &lt; x:\n      low = mid + 1\n    else:\n      high = mid - 1\n\n  return -1\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60]\nx = 40\nprint(binary(l,x))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Recursive Binary Search\n\ndef binary(l, x, low, high):\n  if low &gt; high:\n    return -1\n  mid = (low + high) // 2\n  if l[mid] == x:\n    return mid\n  elif l[mid] &lt; x:\n    return binary(l, x, mid + 1, high)\n  else:\n    return binary(l, x, low, mid - 1)\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60]\nx = 50\n\nprint(binary(l, x, 0, len(l) - 1))</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Bineay Search for Unsorted List</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1\n\naux_space = []\n\ndef make_aux(arr, n):\n  global aux_space\n  for i in range(n):\n    aux_space.append(arr[i])\n\n  aux_space.sort()\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 9, 10, 22, 54, 21, 29]\nmake_aux(l, len(l))\nprint(binary(aux_space, 9, 0, len(aux_space) - 1))\nprint(aux_space)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2\n\ndef binary_search(arr, target):\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n\n    while left &lt;= right:\n        mid = left + (right - left) // 2 # avoiding the Overflow\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            return mid\n        elif arr[mid] &lt; target:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid - 1\n    return -1\n\narr = [3, 6, 1, 9, 4, 2]\narr.sort()\nres = binary_search(arr, 3)\nprint(res)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 3\n\ndef findPeak(nums):\n  left, right = 0 ,len(nums) - 1\n\n  while left &lt; right:\n    mid = left + (right - left) // 2\n    if nums[mid] &lt; nums[mid + 1]:\n      left = mid + 1\n    else:\n      right = mid\n  return left\n\nnums = [1, 2, 1, 3, 5, 6, 4]\nprint(findPeak(nums))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Analysis of Binary Search</h3>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Index of First Occurrence : Sorted Order</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [1, 10, 20, 10, 20, 30, 30, 10 ]</p>\n</div>\n<p>x = 20</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> 2</p>\n</div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>For the first occurrence of a number</h3>\n<p>1. If (high &gt;= low)</p>\n<p>2. Calculate mid = low + (high - low)/2;</p>\n<p>3. If ((mid == 0 || x &gt; arr[mid-1]) &amp;&amp; arr[mid] == x) : return mid;</p>\n<p>4. Else if (x &gt; arr[mid]) : return first(arr, (mid + 1), high, x, n);</p>\n<p>5. Else : return first(arr, low, (mid -1), x, n);</p>\n<p>6. Otherwise return -1;</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive : Unsorted &amp; Sorted Order\n\ndef firstOcc(arr, n, x):\n  for i in range(0, n):\n    if arr[i] == x:\n      return i\n  return - 1\n\nl = [1, 10, 20, 10, 20, 30, 30, 10]\nn = len(l)\nx = 20\nprint(firstOcc(l, n, x))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient : Using Recursion\n\ndef firstOcc(arr, low, high, x, n):\n  if low &gt; high:\n    return -1\n\n  if(high &gt;= low):\n    mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n    if((mid == 0 or x &gt; arr[mid - 1]) and arr[mid] == x):\n      return mid\n    elif(x &gt; arr[mid]):\n      return firstOcc(arr, (mid + 1), high, x, n)\n    else:\n      return firstOcc(arr, low, (mid - 1), x, n)\n\n  return -1\n\nl = [10, 10, 20, 30, 40, 40, 40, 40]\n\nn = len(l)\nx = 20\nprint(firstOcc(l, 0, n - 1, x, n))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient using Iteration\n\ndef first(arr, n, x):\n  low = 0\n  high = n - 1\n  while low &lt;= high:\n    mid = (low + high) // 2\n    if x &gt; arr[mid]:\n      low = mid + 1\n    elif x &lt; arr[mid]:\n      high = mid - 1\n    else:\n      if mid == 0 or x &gt; arr[mid - 1]:\n        return mid\n      else:\n        high = mid - 1\n\n  return -1\n\nl = [10, 10, 20, 30, 40, 40, 40, 40]\nn = len(l)\nx = 20\nprint(first(l, n, x))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Index of Last Occurrence : Sorted Order</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [1, 10, 20, 10, 20, 30, 30, 10 ]</p>\n</div>\n<p>x = 20</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> 4</p>\n</div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>For the Last occurrence of a number</h3>\n<p>1. if (high &gt;= low)</p>\n<p>2. calculate mid = low + (high - low)/2;</p>\n<p>3. if( ( mid == n-1 || x &lt; arr[mid+1]) &amp;&amp; arr[mid] == x ) : return mid;</p>\n<p>4. else if(x &lt; arr[mid]) : return last(arr, low, (mid -1), x, n);</p>\n<p>5. else : return last(arr, (mid + 1), high, x, n); </p>\n<p>6. otherwise return -1;</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive : Unsorted &amp; Sorted Orders\n\ndef findLastOccurrence(arr, n, x):\n    last = -1\n    for i in range(n):\n        if arr[i] == x:\n            last = i\n\n    if last != -1:\n        print(\"Last Occurrence = \", last)\n    else:\n        print(\"Not Found\")\n\nl = [10, 20, 30, 20, 30, 40, 40, 40]\nn = len(l)\nx = 30\nfindLastOccurrence(l, n, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient : Using Recursion\n\ndef last(arr, low, high, x, n):\n\tif (high &gt;= low):\n\t\tmid = low + (high - low) // 2\n\t\tif ((mid == n - 1 or x &lt; arr[mid + 1]) and arr[mid] == x):\n\t\t\treturn mid\n\t\telif (x &lt; arr[mid]):\n\t\t\treturn last(arr, low, (mid - 1), x, n)\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\treturn last(arr, (mid + 1), high, x, n)\n\n\treturn -1\n\n\narr = [1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 8]\nn = len(arr)\n\nx = 8\nprint(\"Last Occurrence = \", last(arr, 0, n - 1, x, n))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Count Occurences in a Sorted Array</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> l = [10, 20, 20, 20, 30, 30]</p>\n</div>\n<p>x = 20</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> 3</p>\n</div>\n<p>NOTE :</p>\n<p>Naive Solution : Linear Traversal : O(n)</p>\n<p>Better Solution : Simple Binary search : O(logn + K)</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Better Solution\n\ndef search(nums, target, find_start_index):\n    answer = -1\n    start = 0\n    end = len(nums) - 1\n    while start &lt;= end:\n        mid = start + (end - start) // 2\n        if target &lt; nums[mid]:\n            end = mid - 1\n        elif target &gt; nums[mid]:\n            start = mid + 1\n        else:\n            answer = mid\n            if find_start_index:\n                end = mid - 1\n            else:\n                start = mid + 1\n    return answer\n\ndef count_occurrences(nums, x):\n    first_index = search(nums, x, True)\n    last_index = search(nums, x, False)\n    if first_index != -1 and last_index != -1:\n        return last_index - first_index + 1\n    else:\n        return 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    arr = [1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 8]\n    x = 2\n    c = count_occurrences(arr, x)\n    print(c)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef firstOcc(arr, x):\n  n = len(arr)\n  for i in range(0, n):\n    if arr[i] == x:\n      return i\n  return - 1\n\ndef lastOcc(arr, x):\n  n = len(arr)\n  for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n    if arr[i] == x:\n      return i\n  return -1\n\ndef countOcc(l, x):\n  first = firstOcc(l, x)\n  if first == -1:\n    return 0\n  else:\n    return lastOcc(l, x) - first + 1\n\nl = [10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 20, 30, 30]\nx = 20\nprint(countOcc(l, x))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Count 1's in a Sorted Binary List</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p>Input: arr[] = {1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0}<br>Output: 2<br>Input: arr[] = {1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1}<br>Output: 7<br>Input: arr[] = {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0}<br>Output: 0</p>\n</div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Naive approach:</h3>\n<p> A simple solution is to linearly traverse the array until we find the 1's in the array and keep count of 1s. If the array element becomes 0 then return the count of 1's.</p>\n<p>Time Complexity: O(n)</p>\n<p>Auxiliary Space: O(1)</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Efficient : Count 1's in a sorted binary array using Binary search recursively</h3>\n<p>Do while low &lt;= high:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Calculate mid using low + (high - low) / 2.</li>\n<li>Check if the element at mid index is the last 1</li>\n<li>If the element is not last 1, move the low to right side recursively and return the result received from it.</li>\n<li>Otherwise, move the low to left recursively and return the result received from it.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def countOnes(arr, low, high):\n    if high &gt;= low:\n        mid = low + (high-low)//2\n        if ((mid == high or arr[mid+1] == 0) and (arr[mid] == 1)):\n            return mid+1\n        if arr[mid] == 1:\n            return countOnes(arr, (mid+1), high)\n        return countOnes(arr, low, mid-1)\n\n    return 0\n\narr = [1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0]\nprint(\"Count of 1's in given array is\", countOnes(arr, 0, len(arr)-1))\n\n# Auxiliary Space: O(log(n))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Efficient : Count 1's in a sorted binary array using binary search iteratively</h3>\n<p>Do while low &lt;= high:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Calculate the middle index say mid</li>\n<li>Check if arr[mid] is less than 1 then move the high to left side (i.e, hight = mid - 1)</li>\n<li>If the element is not last 1 then move the low to the right side (i.e, low = mid + 1)</li>\n<li>Check if the element at the middle index is last 1 then return mid + 1</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Otherwise move to low to right (i.e, low = mid + 1)</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def countOnes(arr, n):\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    while (low &lt;= high):\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if ((mid == n - 1 or arr[mid + 1] == 0) and arr[mid] == 1):\n            return mid + 1\n        if (arr[mid] == 0):\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif(arr[mid] == 1):\n            low = mid + 1\n\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    arr = [1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0]\n    n = len(arr)\n    print(\"Count of 1's in given array is \", countOnes(arr, n))\n\n# Auxiliary Space: O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Square Root</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> x = 4<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive\n\ndef sqrtt(x):\n  i = 1\n  while i*i &lt;= x:\n    i += 1\n  return i - 1\n\nprint(sqrtt(4))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient\n\ndef sqrt(x):\n  low = 1\n  high = x\n  ans = -1\n\n  while low &lt;= high:\n    mid = (low + high) // 2\n    msq = mid * mid\n    if msq == x:\n      return mid\n    elif msq &lt; x:\n      low = mid + 1\n      ans = mid\n    else:\n      high = mid - 1\n  return ans\n\nprint(sqrt(4))</code></pre></figure></section>"}